 * reload block + both FillWord calls + tail are byte-identical). Residue is
 * §B15-class: the stride constant-select — original materializes it as
 * beqz; lui-in-delay(shared); j; ori(-0x13000-arm in j delay); ori(-0x1C000)
 * — while our sched1 hoists the shared lui to the function head and reorg
 * then lays else-ori in the beqz delay + rematerialized lui/ori inline (no
 * j). Ternary and if/else forms emit byte-identical output. The hoisted lui
 * also shifts top/stride register roles (a3/a1 vs v0/v1) and batches the
 * three head addiu's. Permuter candidate.
